examples.question_text:
Write the vector $\underset{\sim}{v}$ as (a) a column vector and (b) in component form. Each grid square represents one unit.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{gridColour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[xstep=7mm,ystep=7mm,color=gridColour,very thin] (-2,-2) grid (4,3);
\draw[<->,black] (-2.4,0)--(4.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-2.4)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \t in {-2,-1,1,2,3,4} {\draw[black] (\t,0.08)--(\t,-0.08);\path (\t,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\t$};}
\foreach \t in {-2,-1,1,2,3} {\draw[black] (0.08,\t)--(-0.08,\t);\path (0,\t) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\t$};}
\draw[->,thick,black] (3,2)--(-1,-1);
\path (1,1.2) node[above right] {$\underset{\sim}{v}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Read the movement from tail to tip: four units left and three units down. Both components are negative.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{gridColour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\definecolor{horizontalColour}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{verticalColour}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[xstep=7mm,ystep=7mm,color=gridColour,very thin] (-2,-2) grid (4,3);
\draw[->,thick,black] (3,2)--(-1,-1);
\draw[->,thick,color=horizontalColour] (3,2)--(-1,2);
\draw[->,thick,color=verticalColour] (-1,2)--(-1,-1);
\path (1,2) node[above] {$-4$};
\path (-1,0.5) node[left] {$-3$};
\path (1,0.1) node[right] {$\underset{\sim}{v}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) $\underset{\sim}{v}=\begin{pmatrix}-4\\-3\end{pmatrix}$

(b) $\underset{\sim}{v}=-4\underset{\sim}{i}-3\underset{\sim}{j}$
